          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तनाव",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तनाव — tanāv — \"stress; tension\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नौकरी के तनाव से अरुण की नींद चली गई। naukrī ke tanāv se Aruṇ kī nīnd calī gaī. The stress of his job has cost Arun his sleep."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तनाव (tanāv) is probably a noun built on the root of tānnā, \"to stretch, pull, tighten\", which CDIAL lists under Sanskrit tānáyati (CDIAL 5762): a rope pulled tight, and then a mind. CDIAL gives no row for tanāv itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
